 "id": "2026-11-25-two-coasts-flood-thanksgiving",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Record water in San Francisco. Major flooding in Charleston. And Thanksgiving is next."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "San Francisco first. On Tuesday, the gauge at Crissy Field hit eight point two three feet, the National Weather Service says. That broke a November record from nineteen eighty-two. King tides, a storm surge and warm El Niño water combined, reports say."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then Charleston, on the East Coast. Wednesday morning, its harbor gauge topped eight feet, The Weather Channel reports. That is major flood stage. It held for almost two hours. Downtown roads closed, and CNN says the evening high tide could bring more."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Next, New Jersey and Delaware. CNN says the biggest threat comes with Thanksgiving morning's high tide, around eight in Atlantic City. Fox Weather reports South Jersey may see its highest water since Superstorm Sandy. Forecasters also warn of damaging gusts."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Jersey Shore see its highest water since Sandy? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
