 "upload": {
  "title": "San Francisco Sets a Tide Record, Then Charleston Floods #shorts",
  "description": "Coastal flooding hit both U.S. coasts in Thanksgiving week. On Tuesday the Crissy Field gauge in San Francisco reached 8.23 feet, breaking a November record from 1982, according to the National Weather Service. On Wednesday morning Charleston's harbor gauge topped 8 feet, major flood stage, for almost two hours, The Weather Channel reports. CNN says Thursday morning's high tide is the biggest threat for New Jersey and Delaware, and Fox Weather reports South Jersey may see its highest water since Superstorm Sandy.\n\nSources: National Weather Service via KQED, CBS San Francisco and Local News Matters; The Weather Channel; CNN; Fox Weather (based on search-result excerpts). Flood areas on the map are approximate and illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #kingtides #coastalflooding #thanksgiving",
